      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Linear Dy4 cluster with nitrate-capped peripheral Dy sites. Room-temperature χT matches four Dy(III) ions and decreases on cooling, consistent with mJ depopulation and possible antiferromagnetic interactions. Magnetization at 1.8 K does not saturate. Zero-field AC data show QTM without a χ'' maximum; even under applied dc field, 1 shows only a high-frequency χ'' signal without a maximum and is not a field-induced SMM, unlike acetate analogue 2. CASSCF indicates easy-plane anisotropy at central Dy1.",
